-- title:
--   Galois model of X_H(M) over K(j) in characteristic 2
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup, and let $\Gamma_H(M)$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ whose associated unit (the reduction mod $M$ of the lower-right entry, a unit by `gamma0Units`) lies in $H$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $2$, and let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by all quotients $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ (regarded inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$) whose $q$-expansions are given by integral power series $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$, with coefficientwise reduction $\bar p_g \ne 0$ in $K[[q]]$. Let $x \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC K`, the reduction to $K$ of $q^{-1}\cdot E_4^3\eta^{-24}$, i.e. of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}+744+\cdots$ of the modular invariant $j$. Then there exist a field $L$ (in the same universe as $K$), a $K$-algebra structure on $L$, and a $K$-algebra homomorphism $\iota \colon F \to L$ such that $L$ is finite-dimensional and Galois over the intermediate field $K(\iota x)$ generated by $\iota x$, and such that for every place $P$ of $L$ over $K$ — a valuation subring of $L$, distinct from $L$, containing the image of $K$ and a principal ideal ring — with $\mathrm{ord}_P(\iota x) > 0$ one has $\mathrm{ord}_P(\iota x) \mid 12$; here $\mathrm{ord}_P$ is minus the logarithm of the adic valuation attached to $P$.
--
--   This is an Igusa-style statement that the reduction mod $2$ of the function field of $X_H(M)$ ($M$ odd) sits inside a finite Galois extension $L$ of the rational subfield generated by $j$, with all ramification indices above the place $j = 0$ dividing $12$. It feeds the local analysis at the elliptic point $j = 0$ in characteristic $2$, being cited in the divisibility bound [`ModularCurve.ord_dvd_twelve_div_sub_one_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ord_dvd_twelve_div_sub_one_of_ord_pos_x1FunctionFieldC_of_lt_five) and in the degree/double-coset counting inequality [`ModularCurve.two_mul_index_le_sum_ordDiff_D_add_natCard_doubleCoset_of_lt_five`](thm.html#ModularCurve.two_mul_index_le_sum_ordDiff_D_add_natCard_doubleCoset_of_lt_five).
